# Crime Novelist: "Whenever you sacrifice an artifact, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature and add {R}." Under Mycosynth
# Lattice the Novelist is an artifact, and Ashnod's Altar sacrifices it for its own mana. "Whenever you sacrifice" looks back
# in time (CR 603.10a), so the Novelist sees its own sacrifice; the sacrifice pays a mana ability's cost, so the trigger is a
# triggered mana ability that resolves at once (CR 605.1b, 605.4a): {C}{C} from the Altar and {R} from the Novelist, with
# nothing on the stack. The counter goes nowhere: the Novelist is gone (CR 400.7), so the {R} it produced is what shows it.
# Turn 1: Mountain and Sol Ring pay for the Novelist. Turn 3: two Mountains, two Mox Rubies and Sol Ring pay for the Lattice.
# Turn 5: Sol Ring and a Mox pay for the Altar, which then sacrifices the Novelist.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Sol Ring
Crime Novelist
Mycosynth Lattice
Ashnod's Altar
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

